      en: "The Old Path Military Trail is a significant historical site located within the Wong Nai Chung Gap in Hong Kong, offering a poignant look into the city's defense during World War II. This trail is a crucial section of the Wong Nai Chung Gap Heritage Trail, where some of the most intense fighting occurred during the Battle of Hong Kong in December 1941. As you walk along the path, you will encounter well-preserved bunkers and pillboxes that once served as strategic defensive positions for Allied forces. Informative plaques along the route provide detailed historical context about the movements of the Japanese army and the heroic resistance of the local defenders. The trail is not only a historical classroom but also a pleasant hiking route, offering a mix of dense forest paths and glimpses of the modern cityscape beyond the greenery. It serves as a lasting memorial to the soldiers who fought on these rugged slopes, making it a must-visit for history enthusiasts and nature lovers alike who wish to explore the strategic heights that once decided the fate of the territory.",
